                        "glosses": [
                            "Pain in the bones, or seemingly in the bones."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e62e20fe-2674-41d5-9615-d16459a15797",
                                "sense_id": "36e82fce-720e-3fa3-926e-66a4da94b838",
                                "text": "After this, the vengeance on the whole camp! or rather, the bone-ache! for that, methinks, is the curse dependent on those that war for a placket."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a592ac77-fec0-442d-a76a-88c2a85250e7",
                                "sense_id": "36e82fce-720e-3fa3-926e-66a4da94b838",
                                "text": "The blueberries grew far away and the Old Lady had many a tramp after them. Sometimes her bones ached at night because of it; but what cared the Old Lady for that? Bone ache is easier to endure than soul ache; and the Old Lady’s soul had stopped aching for the first time in many a year."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2342483-e1db-4b52-8022-b395eeca92d3",
                                "sense_id": "36e82fce-720e-3fa3-926e-66a4da94b838",
                                "text": "\"Well, sorcerer?\" growled the Norman. \"Nay, not well,\" replied Catweazle shivering miserably, \"I have the bone-ache.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
